WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:03.090
- [Mark] All right, Ally.

00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:03.923
- Yes.

00:00:03.923 --> 00:00:04.756
- [Mark] Ally, where
are you from originally?

00:00:04.756 --> 00:00:05.589
Where'd you grow up?

00:00:05.589 --> 00:00:06.422
- Alaska.

00:00:06.422 --> 00:00:07.255
- [Mark] Alaska?

00:00:07.255 --> 00:00:08.410
- Yes.
- Really?

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:09.951
And tell me about your childhood,

00:00:09.951 --> 00:00:12.360
do you have both your parents growing up?

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.550
- No, I had my mom and my
dad was around 'til I was two

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:20.500
and then he disappeared
from my life until,

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.960
first time I saw him
again was when I was 14.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.060
- [Mark] Okay, and how was your childhood?

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:31.050
- Well, on the outside
looking in, I had everything.

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:33.800
All the opportunities, my
grandparents were well-to-do.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:37.390
But my mom was a cocaine
addict until I was eight

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:39.160
and then she got clean.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:44.160
But my sister, she's four and
a half years older than me,

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:49.550
she was sexually molested
by her Campfire teacher

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:53.993
that the school had for the
summer put on, and quite badly.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:01:01.030
And so kids, how they cope
with that, they reenact things.

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:04.647
And so from the time I was three years old

00:01:04.647 --> 00:01:06.160
'til nine years old,

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:08.140
I was sexually molested by my sister

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:10.850
and any neighborhood kids
that she could involve.

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:12.100
- [Mark] Really?

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.053
- Uh-huh.
- Yeah.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:19.523
- Very sexually molested.
(laughing)

00:01:21.365 --> 00:01:22.620
- [Mark] And this went on for how long?

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:24.327
- From three to nine.
- Three to nine.

00:01:24.327 --> 00:01:26.690
- And the reason it
stopped when I was nine

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:28.627
is 'cause that's when my
sister ran away from home

00:01:28.627 --> 00:01:30.123
and she became a prostitute.

00:01:31.615 --> 00:01:32.448
- [Mark] And where is she today?

00:01:32.448 --> 00:01:35.160
- She today is in North Pole, Alaska.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:40.160
And she has kids and
she's doing a lot better.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:42.133
She still has a lot of issues.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:48.193
She's drug addict like we all
are in my family pretty much.

00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:54.767
But she's not really prostituting
anymore for the most part,

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:59.355
but for drugs she might whatever.

00:01:59.355 --> 00:02:00.188
(Mark chuckles)
- Yeah

00:02:00.188 --> 00:02:01.700
- She does what she does.
- Right.

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:02.533
- But...

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:09.290
She was always the outcast in the family

00:02:09.290 --> 00:02:10.530
and I was considered the good kid

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.980
but I was the one who was always in jail.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.680
I've spent half my life in prison.

00:02:16.783 --> 00:02:21.040
I wanted to be self sufficient,
well let me back up.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:25.000
So at 11 years old, I got
addicted to cocaine, I'd snort it.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:27.980
And then by 12 years old, I
was addicted to crack cocaine.

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:29.600
- [Mark] Who introduced you to that?

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:31.290
- That would be one of my uncle's friends

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:33.724
at a Christmas party at
my grandmother's house.

00:02:33.724 --> 00:02:35.140
(Ally chuckles)
- Great.

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:37.483
- And that was, Mike Chatly was his name.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:42.060
And we would sit down in
the basement and play pool.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:43.830
I loved hangin' out with
my aunts and my uncles

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.490
'cause they let me drink and stuff,

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:46.870
it was a different time back in the '80s.

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:47.850
- [Mark] Yes.

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:52.050
- And so by 12 years old,
I was addicted to crack

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:55.230
and I couldn't function
with kids my age in school.

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:58.100
So I dropped out of school in 7th grade.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:00.963
And so I have basically
a 7th grade education.

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:04.510
I did go back when I was
22 and got my G.E.D.,

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:05.343
but...

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:10.955
I really have no book smarts

00:03:10.955 --> 00:03:11.788
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:03:11.788 --> 00:03:12.650
- From that age.

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:14.860
- [Mark] So where did
your life go from there?

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:18.260
- From there I moved out of my mom's house

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:21.960
and I went, I grew up
in Fairbanks, Alaska.

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:24.220
And when I was eight, my
mom got clean off drugs

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:26.100
and we moved to Anchorage.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:30.940
And so when I was 12 and I
moved out of my mom's house,

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:34.230
I went back to Fairbanks
to stay with my grandmother

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:36.730
and I had a horse and everything.

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:40.540
But was addicted to drugs,
and I couldn't cope there.

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:45.540
So I took off from there
and I met this guy, Ryan,

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:49.440
and we started going out, he
was a few years older than me.

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:50.890
And he had his own place.

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:55.680
And he was weird.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:00.130
He didn't physically abuse me
like hitting me all the time,

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:02.200
but he would do weird stuff.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:04.750
If I wouldn't have sex with
him, he'd fuck my legs.

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:11.550
He would put plastic bags over
my head and poke holes in it

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:12.913
just to watch me suffer.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:17.963
He would do really weird stuff to me.

00:04:19.420 --> 00:04:23.180
But I got away from him and
I went back to Anchorage

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:25.000
to be with my mom.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:27.760
And I was like 15 at this time.

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:32.320
And my mom and my stepdad
did ballroom and line dancing

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:34.620
so I grew up doing that too.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:39.620
And my mom had a junior team
and they would travel all over

00:04:39.833 --> 00:04:42.730
the states and stuff competing and stuff.

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:46.530
And my mom also had a
dance apparel business,

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:49.150
and it's called Showstoppers Dance Wear.

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:52.700
And so she had me working for her

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:54.490
while her junior team,

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:56.890
I think they were in Paris or something

00:04:56.890 --> 00:04:58.000
for a dance competition.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:02.480
And my sister came by and we emptied out

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:03.710
my mom's cash register
(Ally chuckles)

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:05.220
and we went and got a bunch of crack

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:07.590
and we were partyin' at the house

00:05:07.590 --> 00:05:10.210
and my sister went outside
for some odd reason

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:11.320
at like four in the morning.

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:13.580
And I heard her scream
so I went running out,

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:15.060
and there was Ryan.

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:19.220
And he snatched me up and
took me to Valdez, Alaska.

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:24.098
And for like two weeks he had me in a tent

00:05:24.098 --> 00:05:28.710
in Valdez, Alaska at a campground,
and it was my birthday.

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:30.760
And I wanted to call my mom
and tell her I was alive

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:33.190
because nobody knew what happened to me.

00:05:33.190 --> 00:05:35.400
And he got upset by it and he was drunk

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:36.450
and he put a gun to my head

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:38.550
and somebody seen it and called the cops.

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:40.870
So for like three hours they tried get him

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:42.560
to take the gun away
from him but he didn't.

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:45.720
He cocked it and pulled
the trigger, and it jammed.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:47.240
And so they took him to jail.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:50.903
And from there, I ran away to Hawaii.

00:05:53.231 --> 00:05:57.790
And in Hawaii, I'm a crack head,

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.290
and they didn't have much crack there.

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:01.622
They had ice or about to.
(laughing)

00:06:01.622 --> 00:06:06.290
So I started doing meth.

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:08.170
And I quit smoking crack.

00:06:08.170 --> 00:06:13.170
And I started going from Maui to Oahu.

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:16.880
I would buy a couple
ounces and go back to Maui

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:18.850
and sell 'em and then go back.

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:23.100
And I had a boyfriend
who was on work furlough,

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:24.260
which is you're in prison

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:26.750
but you can go out during the day to work.

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:29.300
And he's much older than
me, 18 years older than me.

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:31.210
And his name was Al.

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:34.910
And his actual name is
Louelle and he's Hawaiian.

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:39.910
And one day when I was in
Oahu picking up my stuff,

00:06:40.110 --> 00:06:42.620
I was pregnant by this
time with my first child.

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:47.620
I was 19 or 20 by this time.

00:06:48.190 --> 00:06:52.360
And the guy seen a
picture of Al in my wallet

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:53.707
and he was like, "Why
do you have a picture

00:06:53.707 --> 00:06:54.540
"of this guy in your wallet?"

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:56.680
And I said, "That's
the father of my baby."

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:58.740
And he's like, "Oh shit." (Ally chuckles)

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:01.707
He's like, "No, no, no, no,
I'ma put you back on a plane

00:07:01.707 --> 00:07:03.620
"and from this moment on,
we don't know each other."

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:05.220
And I'm like, "Why?" (Ally chuckles)

00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:07.260
And he's like, "Because I don't
wanna get my throat slit."

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:08.800
And I was like, "What?"

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:10.360
And I had no idea at the time

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:12.558
that the guy I was pregnant by

00:07:12.558 --> 00:07:17.558
was a huge, very well known
drug dealer in Hawaii.

00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:22.340
And (Ally chuckles) I just had no idea.

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:25.040
I thought that I was
somethin', but I was nothin'.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:27.520
And anyway, he got out of jail

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:32.440
and (sniffling) my life
with him was crazy.

00:07:32.440 --> 00:07:35.790
He was a huge drug dealer

00:07:35.790 --> 00:07:36.623
and...

00:07:39.670 --> 00:07:43.940
Basically I stayed holed up in a house,

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:46.140
pregnant and I never seen him.

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:49.140
His runners would bring
me food and whatnot.

00:07:49.140 --> 00:07:51.593
And I was kind of just goin' crazy.

00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:56.063
But I was crazy for him.

00:07:58.581 --> 00:08:01.453
He tried to run me down.

00:08:02.600 --> 00:08:04.200
Or I tried to run him down one time

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:05.340
when he was trying to get away from me.

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:08.250
But basically, the cops,

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:10.220
because they knew who I was with,

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:11.680
anytime I was walking down the street,

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:13.730
they would literally arrest me,

00:08:13.730 --> 00:08:15.987
take me to jail for no reason.

00:08:15.987 --> 00:08:17.720
And they couldn't hold
me more than three days

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:18.870
but they would interrogate me

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:20.743
and try to get me to give him up.

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:24.148
When I gave birth to my kid,

00:08:24.148 --> 00:08:27.680
I gave birth with cops
in my delivery room.

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:29.540
He couldn't come to the hospital.

00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:31.543
And then they took my baby away from me.

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:35.233
All because of who he was.

00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:40.040
And I had no chance of
getting my kid back,

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:41.940
which I didn't know at the time,

00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:43.160
but they didn't call.

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:46.270
I didn't wanna tell my
family that I lost my kid.

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:48.410
So I lied and I acted like I had him.

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:51.740
But my mom and my
grandmother came to Hawaii

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:53.970
to surprise me one day and meet the baby

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:55.520
and they found me walking down the street

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:59.180
and I was probably like
90 pounds, all strung out.

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:02.140
And they wanted to know
where the baby was.

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:03.540
And that's when I told 'em I lost it.

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:05.250
My grandmother had to sue

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:07.550
the state of Hawaii to get him back

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:10.879
'cause they had an adoption ring going on.

00:09:10.879 --> 00:09:12.210
(sniffling)

00:09:12.210 --> 00:09:16.950
And she did get him and
she has him to this day.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:18.323
When I was in Hawaii,

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:21.740
my babies dad, he was wanted obviously.

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:26.490
And I wanted to get off
the island with him somehow

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:28.587
and I just started thinking,

00:09:28.587 --> 00:09:31.815
"Gosh, I could just make
you an I.D. or something."

00:09:31.815 --> 00:09:34.720
And I found out that I
had this amazing knack

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:36.742
for making I.D.'s, I could make I.D.'s.

00:09:36.742 --> 00:09:37.575
(Ally chuckles)

00:09:37.575 --> 00:09:40.760
So I started making I.D.'s
and birth certificates

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:41.760
and Social Security cards

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:44.675
and anything else that I could recreate.

00:09:44.675 --> 00:09:49.210
And in the meantime he got busted.

00:09:49.210 --> 00:09:51.960
And there's a huge story behind that too,

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:54.080
but I guess I don't need
to go into all that.

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:58.020
But the cops on Maui were dirty.

00:09:58.020 --> 00:10:01.610
And I had internal affairs
when I was in jail come

00:10:01.610 --> 00:10:03.390
try to speak to me to
find out what I knew.

00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:05.894
But I didn't know anything at the time.

00:10:05.894 --> 00:10:06.727
I didn't find out 'til later on

00:10:06.727 --> 00:10:09.590
that my baby's dad had some sort

00:10:09.590 --> 00:10:12.530
of indisputable evidence
against the police department

00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:14.550
bringing in drugs,
making contract killings,

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:16.020
things like that.

00:10:16.020 --> 00:10:21.020
And he worried that we
might have to go into hiding

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:25.530
and stuff because when
they were to catch him

00:10:25.530 --> 00:10:26.580
and arrest him,

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:30.292
one cop in particular,
his name was Rocky Silva,

00:10:30.292 --> 00:10:32.373
he would shoot to kill.

00:10:33.340 --> 00:10:36.460
If he found us, he would start shooting,

00:10:36.460 --> 00:10:39.770
and we didn't have to
have a gun or anything.

00:10:39.770 --> 00:10:41.600
He raped one girl
(police sirens blaring)

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:44.398
with a nightstick in the
butt thinking it was me.

00:10:44.398 --> 00:10:46.520
(police sirens blaring)

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:50.070
Just because he had a vendetta against Al

00:10:50.070 --> 00:10:51.923
for having this evidence or whatever.

00:10:52.890 --> 00:10:56.460
A rookie cop was the one
who busted my baby's dad.

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:59.100
Which is why he's still alive right now.

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:00.950
But he's still in prison to this day.

00:11:02.473 --> 00:11:03.530
It's been
(police sirens blaring)

00:11:03.530 --> 00:11:05.713
18 years and he's still in prison.

00:11:07.901 --> 00:11:11.840
He has four first degree attempted murder

00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:14.886
to four police officers and
25 first degree assaults.

00:11:14.886 --> 00:11:16.080
And...

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:21.000
Like I said, internal affairs came

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:22.500
to visit me when I was in jail

00:11:23.470 --> 00:11:25.580
because they wanted to know
what I knew about this evidence

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:27.540
that he had, which I didn't
know anything about, Thank God

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:29.590
'cause I'd probably be dead right now.

00:11:29.590 --> 00:11:33.670
But the reason I went to prison

00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:36.700
is because when I was
trying to make I.D.'s

00:11:36.700 --> 00:11:37.960
for us to get off the island

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:40.420
and I found out that I
was really good at it,

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:43.750
I started thinkin', "Wow I
could do somethin' with this."

00:11:43.750 --> 00:11:47.620
So it was Kmart at the time had this thing

00:11:47.620 --> 00:11:49.580
they called instantaneous credit.

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:52.360
And you could go in with a name,

00:11:52.360 --> 00:11:56.970
a Social Security number, and an address

00:11:56.970 --> 00:12:00.760
and you'd find out if
you were good for credit.

00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:02.840
And if you were, then you
could shop for three days

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:05.780
with that receipt until the
actual card came in the mail.

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:09.160
So I would go rob people's
mailboxes for their information

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:12.650
and then I would go and I
had my little printer setup

00:12:12.650 --> 00:12:15.180
in my car with my inverter

00:12:15.180 --> 00:12:20.180
to make I.D.'s right then and
there if I got the credit.

00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:25.460
So I would do that and then
I started finding checks

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:27.030
in the mail and I started doing that

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:28.440
'cause you can get cash back.

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:32.460
You can write a check out and
return the item the next day

00:12:32.460 --> 00:12:33.560
and get the cash back.

00:12:35.083 --> 00:12:37.095
And it just gradually grew

00:12:37.095 --> 00:12:42.095
until I was rollin' in a 2002 Lexus

00:12:42.760 --> 00:12:46.380
and I was 21 years old.

00:12:46.380 --> 00:12:51.380
I had a kid that I didn't
have because my grandmother

00:12:51.549 --> 00:12:54.457
was at this time battling for him.

00:12:55.820 --> 00:13:00.010
But I was so strung out,
I just was outta control.

00:13:00.010 --> 00:13:03.943
But when I got busted,

00:13:05.896 --> 00:13:08.510
they made a new law just for me basically.

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:10.170
Because when they busted me,

00:13:10.170 --> 00:13:12.640
all they busted me with was
a bunch of unopened mail.

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:15.170
And actually a lot of
people think that's federal

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:18.240
but it's not, it's not federal
until you open the mail.

00:13:18.240 --> 00:13:21.790
And because it wasn't opened,
they really didn't have much

00:13:21.790 --> 00:13:24.610
but a 30 day thing that
they could get me on.

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:27.320
But the girl that I was busted with,

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:30.610
her statement that she made

00:13:30.610 --> 00:13:33.630
got it to where they made a
whole new law just for me.

00:13:33.630 --> 00:13:34.730
A new identity theft law,

00:13:34.730 --> 00:13:37.835
which they say is worse than manslaughter

00:13:37.835 --> 00:13:39.300
because it's premeditated,

00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:42.870
and it carries up to 20 years per count.

00:13:42.870 --> 00:13:46.150
Well I had 72 charges of that.

00:13:46.150 --> 00:13:51.150
So my first public
pretender, public defender.

00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:55.540
Said I was gonna do 40 years flat, period.

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:57.113
I was only 22 years old.

00:13:58.200 --> 00:13:59.940
I'd never been to jail for anything other

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:03.090
than I had one second degree assault,

00:14:03.090 --> 00:14:06.693
which was bogus too while
I was with my baby's dad.

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:10.810
We were robbed at four in the
morning by three Samoan guys.

00:14:10.810 --> 00:14:13.710
And they came in beating us with bats.

00:14:13.710 --> 00:14:15.330
I was eight and a half months pregnant.

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:18.150
And to make a long story short,

00:14:18.150 --> 00:14:21.100
I slit one guy's throat and
I stabbed the other two.

00:14:21.100 --> 00:14:23.057
In the mean time the second
guy got the knife away from me

00:14:23.057 --> 00:14:24.500
and I grabbed back by the blade

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:26.234
and I cut all my fingertips off.

00:14:26.234 --> 00:14:27.067
(Ally chuckles)

00:14:27.067 --> 00:14:28.913
And so when the cops came

00:14:28.913 --> 00:14:30.980
and I was standing there with the knife,

00:14:30.980 --> 00:14:32.750
and there was blood and there was a circle

00:14:32.750 --> 00:14:34.410
of people all around me,

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:36.750
and all four of us went
to the emergency room.

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:38.805
Me and the three guys that robbed us.

00:14:38.805 --> 00:14:42.085
Because we all had stab wounds.

00:14:42.085 --> 00:14:46.706
And I had passed out or something

00:14:46.706 --> 00:14:49.170
because when I woke up I
was handcuffed to the bed

00:14:49.170 --> 00:14:50.430
and I didn't understand why.

00:14:50.430 --> 00:14:52.000
'Cause I was at home,

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:53.487
I was eight and a half months pregnant,

00:14:53.487 --> 00:14:57.930
I was tiny besides a big
belly and I'm a female.

00:14:57.930 --> 00:15:00.260
And there's three huge Samoan guys

00:15:00.260 --> 00:15:02.670
and I'm handcuffed to the bed.

00:15:02.670 --> 00:15:04.590
And I'm hearing them ask

00:15:04.590 --> 00:15:06.860
if they wanna press charges against me.

00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:11.040
And thank God they said no,
but I went to jail that night.

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:13.110
My baby's dad bailed me out

00:15:13.110 --> 00:15:15.703
for 24 thousand cash an hour later.

00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:20.820
No bail bonds, just $24 thousand cash.

00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:25.170
And I have a second degree
assault on my record

00:15:25.170 --> 00:15:27.420
but I've never been to court for that,

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:29.260
never was convicted of it.

00:15:29.260 --> 00:15:33.060
But I have it on my
record, which is bogus.

00:15:33.060 --> 00:15:34.610
The reason that they took me to jail

00:15:34.610 --> 00:15:36.630
is because of who my baby's dad was.

00:15:36.630 --> 00:15:38.530
That's the only reason.
(police sirens blaring)

00:15:38.530 --> 00:15:41.000
Rocky Silva was the cop on duty that night

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:42.770
that took me to jail.

00:15:42.770 --> 00:15:45.720
This is before my baby's
dad was wanted again.

00:15:45.720 --> 00:15:50.720
Right now he was just still on parole.

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:53.763
He had just done 10 years
in jail and had got out.

00:15:56.267 --> 00:16:01.267
So where was I before I
went back in time to that?

00:16:03.240 --> 00:16:04.560
I was talkin' about...

00:16:05.470 --> 00:16:10.260
Oh yeah, so I gave birth to
my son in the delivery room

00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:14.790
with all the cops in there
tryin' to get my baby's dad.

00:16:14.790 --> 00:16:17.380
But he didn't come to the hospital,

00:16:17.380 --> 00:16:18.763
I lost my baby that day.

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:21.830
My grandmother came.

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:24.870
She was battling for the boy,

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:26.470
oh yeah, and I ended up in jail.

00:16:27.600 --> 00:16:32.030
And the second lawyer
'cause I fired that lawyer,

00:16:32.030 --> 00:16:33.270
also said the same thing.

00:16:33.270 --> 00:16:36.263
I was looking at 40 to 60 years flat.

00:16:36.263 --> 00:16:39.460
So my mom, I love her to death,

00:16:39.460 --> 00:16:42.460
she's never judged me, she's
always been right there for me.

00:16:43.820 --> 00:16:46.980
She had a fundraiser
with her dance students

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:50.573
and they raised up $10 thousand
to get me a real lawyer.

00:16:53.960 --> 00:16:56.403
This whole time in Hawaii really,

00:16:57.832 --> 00:17:00.090
my whole family was behind me

00:17:00.090 --> 00:17:03.370
and they lost everything pretty much.

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:06.140
My grandparents, the money that they spent

00:17:06.140 --> 00:17:07.360
to sue the state of Hawaii

00:17:07.360 --> 00:17:10.400
and get my son pretty
much killed their business

00:17:10.400 --> 00:17:12.033
that they had for 55 years.

00:17:14.490 --> 00:17:15.960
They eventually had to shut down

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:17.910
'cause they couldn't afford it anymore.

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:23.113
My mom put everything she
had into getting me a lawyer,

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:29.430
which was great, I only
ended up getting charged

00:17:29.430 --> 00:17:33.170
with five of those identity
thefts in the first degree.

00:17:33.170 --> 00:17:36.260
And they carried 20 years per count,

00:17:36.260 --> 00:17:38.905
so that's 100 years plus
five credit card thefts

00:17:38.905 --> 00:17:41.480
so that's 122 years is what I got.

00:17:41.480 --> 00:17:43.612
(sniffling)

00:17:43.612 --> 00:17:48.270
I did get out of jail with
a 10 year probation thing,

00:17:48.270 --> 00:17:52.360
with the stipulation that if
I screwed up at all within

00:17:52.360 --> 00:17:56.500
this 10 year period that I had to go back

00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:58.810
and I would do no less than 50 years.

00:17:58.810 --> 00:18:01.110
I had a 50 year mandatory
minimum sentence.

00:18:01.110 --> 00:18:05.780
But the judge could charge me
anywhere from 50 to 122 years,

00:18:05.780 --> 00:18:07.960
which was my max sentence, but no less.

00:18:07.960 --> 00:18:10.060
Well,
(sniffling)

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:11.150
when I got out of jail,

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:15.130
Maui didn't want me to
leave the island of Hawaii

00:18:15.130 --> 00:18:20.130
but my mom had the mayor
and the chief of my tribe,

00:18:24.050 --> 00:18:28.067
I'm Native Alaskan,
Athabaskan Indian Wigan Tribe.

00:18:28.067 --> 00:18:30.020
(sniffling)

00:18:30.020 --> 00:18:32.560
Had them write letters saying
they couldn't legally hold me

00:18:32.560 --> 00:18:35.260
in Hawaii 'cause I'm native to Alaska,

00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:36.527
they can't hold me there.

00:18:36.527 --> 00:18:39.980
And if the probation office
was willing to take me on,

00:18:39.980 --> 00:18:42.330
then they couldn't legally keep me.

00:18:42.330 --> 00:18:45.780
So they gave me a 30 day travel pass

00:18:45.780 --> 00:18:49.182
in which I had to convince
Alaska to take me on

00:18:49.182 --> 00:18:54.182
as a person on probation,
overseeing it for Hawaii,

00:18:55.470 --> 00:18:58.096
which they did, on the
27th day, accept me.

00:18:58.096 --> 00:19:00.917
In the meantime I put
myself into treatment.

00:19:00.917 --> 00:19:02.690
(sniffling)

00:19:02.690 --> 00:19:07.630
And I was okay for three years.

00:19:07.630 --> 00:19:10.093
I graduated treatment and whatnot.

00:19:11.062 --> 00:19:13.461
I was okay for three years,

00:19:13.461 --> 00:19:18.461
and then I screwed up and
started making I.D.'s again,

00:19:19.515 --> 00:19:21.960
started doing drugs and,
(sniffling)

00:19:21.960 --> 00:19:25.230
This time I taught everybody
in Fairbanks how to make I.D.'s

00:19:25.230 --> 00:19:30.010
and there ended up being a huge mail ring

00:19:30.010 --> 00:19:32.160
that they tried to say that
I was the ring leader of

00:19:32.160 --> 00:19:36.291
but I beat that case.

00:19:36.291 --> 00:19:39.270
And I ended up going on a shopping spree

00:19:39.270 --> 00:19:41.240
with my boyfriend in Anchorage.

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:42.160
(sniffling)

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:42.993
For three days.

00:19:42.993 --> 00:19:45.930
And it ended with me feeling
like I needed to go home

00:19:45.930 --> 00:19:49.290
'cause by this time I was
not going to probation,

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:52.170
not checking in, and I
was a wanted fugitive

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:53.860
out of Hawaii at this point.

00:19:53.860 --> 00:19:56.670
And I knew I was screwed, if
I got caught I was going back.

00:19:56.670 --> 00:19:57.770
I was not gonna
(sniffling)

00:19:57.770 --> 00:19:59.301
do less than 50 years.

00:19:59.301 --> 00:20:03.830
And so I was scared, I
wanted to go back home

00:20:03.830 --> 00:20:05.883
and just stay holed up in my house.

00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:10.080
And my boyfriend for
whatever reason decided

00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:12.177
to publicly beat me up.

00:20:12.177 --> 00:20:15.170
Just pulled me out of the car
and start whoopin' my ass.

00:20:15.170 --> 00:20:17.980
And somebody called the cops.

00:20:17.980 --> 00:20:19.420
Well on our way to Fairbanks of course,

00:20:19.420 --> 00:20:20.930
I made like four I.D.'s for him

00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:23.672
'cause all of the checks
we had were in guys's names

00:20:23.672 --> 00:20:24.780
(sniffling)

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:26.920
And
(Ally chuckling)

00:20:26.920 --> 00:20:28.614
it's not funny but it is kind of funny.

00:20:28.614 --> 00:20:31.070
I had a printer of course in my car

00:20:31.070 --> 00:20:32.608
so I could print out
the I.D.'s and whatnot.

00:20:32.608 --> 00:20:33.441
(Ally laughing)

00:20:33.441 --> 00:20:34.850
And I had a sticker which they used

00:20:34.850 --> 00:20:37.310
as evidence against me on my printer

00:20:37.310 --> 00:20:39.075
to show that I had no compassion

00:20:39.075 --> 00:20:40.290
(Ally laughing)
or empathy

00:20:40.290 --> 00:20:41.290
for what I had done.

00:20:42.350 --> 00:20:44.817
It said, "I don't feel like
myself today, maybe I'm you."

00:20:44.817 --> 00:20:47.100
(Ally laughing)

00:20:47.100 --> 00:20:48.650
And that's not funny but it is.

00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:52.606
But anyway so to make a long story short,

00:20:52.606 --> 00:20:55.760
I got busted and I had
to do my time in Alaska

00:20:55.760 --> 00:20:58.820
for this new identity theft crime I got.

00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:01.589
And before they extradited
me back to Hawaii,

00:21:01.589 --> 00:21:02.540
(sniffling)

00:21:02.540 --> 00:21:04.310
I wouldn't tell them my
name when I got busted

00:21:04.310 --> 00:21:06.070
so they booked me under Jane Doe.

00:21:06.070 --> 00:21:07.657
But about seven days later,

00:21:07.657 --> 00:21:08.490
I don't know why it took so long,

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:10.880
maybe their fingerprint thing
was broken or something,

00:21:10.880 --> 00:21:13.480
but it took 'em about a week
to figure out who I was.

00:21:13.480 --> 00:21:15.760
But I heard when they said my last name,

00:21:15.760 --> 00:21:17.763
I knew it was over for me.

00:21:17.763 --> 00:21:22.763
So I got new charges in Alaska

00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:25.866
and then I was waiting to be
extradited back to Hawaii.

00:21:25.866 --> 00:21:26.699
(sniffling)

00:21:26.699 --> 00:21:29.020
And I did my three years in Alaska

00:21:29.020 --> 00:21:31.141
and I was waiting to be
extradited back to Hawaii.

00:21:31.141 --> 00:21:33.510
I talked to my lawyer in Hawaii

00:21:33.510 --> 00:21:36.190
and he said that he had cut me a deal

00:21:36.190 --> 00:21:38.340
for a 30 year flat sentence.

00:21:38.340 --> 00:21:41.200
So I gave my son up for
adoption to my grandmother.

00:21:41.200 --> 00:21:43.900
'Cause up until this
time she just had him.

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:46.283
I had not lost my parental
rights or anything.

00:21:48.300 --> 00:21:50.620
But I gave him up for adoption to her

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:52.870
because I didn't think
I was gonna get out.

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:55.714
So for three years I just
mentally prepared myself

00:21:55.714 --> 00:21:59.623
to not get out 'til I was an old person.

00:22:03.999 --> 00:22:05.210
(Ally chuckling)

00:22:05.210 --> 00:22:07.720
So two weeks before I was supposed

00:22:07.720 --> 00:22:09.370
to get extradited back to Hawaii,

00:22:09.370 --> 00:22:11.190
the in house P.O. comes up to me

00:22:11.190 --> 00:22:13.550
and tells me she wants to
talk to me in the office

00:22:13.550 --> 00:22:15.757
and I thought, "Oh my God,
they're gonna take me early

00:22:15.757 --> 00:22:17.040
"or something, this is awful."

00:22:17.040 --> 00:22:17.873
(sniffling)

00:22:17.873 --> 00:22:19.127
And she says, "What would you do

00:22:19.127 --> 00:22:20.880
"if you were to get out today?"

00:22:20.880 --> 00:22:23.347
And I said, "Why are you
making me tell you that?

00:22:23.347 --> 00:22:24.327
"I don't wanna think about that.

00:22:24.327 --> 00:22:26.220
"I don't wanna think about that."

00:22:26.220 --> 00:22:29.320
I stopped taking visits from
anybody, not family nothing.

00:22:29.320 --> 00:22:31.890
I just would call my son
on the phone, that was it.

00:22:31.890 --> 00:22:35.788
I totally said goodbye
to the outside world.

00:22:35.788 --> 00:22:38.542
And I mentally had to prepare myself.

00:22:38.542 --> 00:22:40.203
It's a long time.

00:22:41.840 --> 00:22:44.930
I like being free, I don't
wanna be locked up in a cage

00:22:44.930 --> 00:22:46.600
like an animal anymore.

00:22:46.600 --> 00:22:48.790
I get really bad anxiety
just thinking about it.

00:22:48.790 --> 00:22:49.833
Really bad P.T.S.D.

00:22:52.761 --> 00:22:57.761
But she made me tell her
anyway, which I was upset about.

00:22:59.010 --> 00:23:00.887
But I told her and she's like, "Well good,

00:23:00.887 --> 00:23:02.827
"you have to go by
exactly what you just said

00:23:02.827 --> 00:23:05.510
"because you're getting out in two weeks."

00:23:05.510 --> 00:23:06.343
I said, "What?"

00:23:06.343 --> 00:23:08.589
And she's like, "Hawaii's
giving you a second chance."

00:23:08.589 --> 00:23:13.589
And so I don't know why but my
first reaction was not happy.

00:23:13.640 --> 00:23:17.470
I was probably in shock obviously

00:23:17.470 --> 00:23:19.390
but I was actually disappointed.

00:23:19.390 --> 00:23:22.060
I was like, "What?"
(Ally laughing)

00:23:22.060 --> 00:23:25.810
I gave up my kid, what do
you mean I'm getting out?

00:23:25.810 --> 00:23:26.830
I was so excited to go to Hawaii

00:23:26.830 --> 00:23:28.742
'cause I could smoke
cigarettes in jail there.

00:23:28.742 --> 00:23:30.340
(Ally laughing and sniffling)

00:23:30.340 --> 00:23:33.630
Stupid stuff, but it took about
24 hours and then it hit me.

00:23:33.630 --> 00:23:35.420
And I was like, "Oh my
God, I'm getting out."

00:23:35.420 --> 00:23:37.220
And I called my grandparents
and I told them.

00:23:37.220 --> 00:23:39.613
And my grandmother was like, "Oh no."

00:23:39.613 --> 00:23:40.880
She was like, "What?"

00:23:40.880 --> 00:23:42.907
She was like, "You do so well in jail.

00:23:42.907 --> 00:23:44.457
"Don't get me wrong, I'm
glad you're getting out.

00:23:44.457 --> 00:23:47.174
"But you excel in prison,

00:23:47.174 --> 00:23:50.677
"and soon as you have your own free will,

00:23:50.677 --> 00:23:52.610
"you just screw up."

00:23:52.610 --> 00:23:53.443
And then I'm like, "Wow."

00:23:53.443 --> 00:23:54.867
And she's like, "And you don't
just screw up a little bit,

00:23:54.867 --> 00:23:56.510
"you screw up bad."
(Ally laughing)

00:23:56.510 --> 00:23:57.830
And I'm like, "Yeah."

00:23:57.830 --> 00:23:59.626
So,
(sniffling)

00:23:59.626 --> 00:24:03.973
one of the people that I had
hurt doing identity theft,

00:24:05.600 --> 00:24:07.583
sorry to back up a little bit.

00:24:08.570 --> 00:24:12.410
In Hawaii when I first
started doing these crimes.

00:24:12.410 --> 00:24:15.778
I didn't care who I did it to.

00:24:15.778 --> 00:24:18.590
I was there to take your money.

00:24:18.590 --> 00:24:22.480
And a lady came, I had several people,

00:24:22.480 --> 00:24:25.185
almost 100 people take the
stand at my arraignment

00:24:25.185 --> 00:24:27.713
just to make sure I wasn't
getting out of jail.

00:24:29.061 --> 00:24:33.000
And one of the ladies was a lady

00:24:33.000 --> 00:24:36.324
that I remembered very well at the time,

00:24:36.324 --> 00:24:38.070
spending her money.
(Ally sniffling)

00:24:38.070 --> 00:24:39.130
I had put her on the street

00:24:39.130 --> 00:24:40.670
and she was a single mother of five.

00:24:40.670 --> 00:24:41.773
Her husband had died.

00:24:43.210 --> 00:24:44.160
And...

00:24:46.000 --> 00:24:48.150
That has stayed with me forever

00:24:48.150 --> 00:24:52.873
because I just couldn't
believe I did that to somebody.

00:24:55.410 --> 00:24:59.160
So when I did start doing
identity theft again,

00:24:59.160 --> 00:25:02.840
I this time decided that I was
going to stalk the obituaries

00:25:02.840 --> 00:25:04.800
and hit dead people instead.

00:25:04.800 --> 00:25:08.600
'Cause I didn't want to screw
up anybody who was alive.

00:25:08.600 --> 00:25:10.519
And although that sounds
really morbid now to me,

00:25:10.519 --> 00:25:11.352
(Ally sniffling)

00:25:11.352 --> 00:25:14.700
at the time I felt like
I was being very kind.

00:25:14.700 --> 00:25:16.329
And I justified it by
(Ally sniffling)

00:25:16.329 --> 00:25:19.300
the fact that I wouldn't
just do any dead person.

00:25:19.300 --> 00:25:21.800
I picked on dead people that
didn't have any next of kin

00:25:21.800 --> 00:25:23.240
who's money was pretty much in probate,

00:25:23.240 --> 00:25:26.414
which I consider a black
hole for the government

00:25:26.414 --> 00:25:27.890
to take your money.

00:25:27.890 --> 00:25:29.974
So I didn't feel like
(Ally sniffling)

00:25:29.974 --> 00:25:32.513
I was doing anything very wrong.

00:25:33.374 --> 00:25:38.374
I felt like our nation or our America,

00:25:40.260 --> 00:25:44.328
or whatever, we idolize Robin
Hood and things like that.

00:25:44.328 --> 00:25:47.700
But yet you grow up and be like that.

00:25:47.700 --> 00:25:49.573
And you get in trouble.

