I'm looking at 10 to 15 years.
(Ally sniffling)

00:37:59.360 --> 00:38:00.193
Yeah.

00:38:02.270 --> 00:38:03.690
- [Mark] And putting this video out

00:38:03.690 --> 00:38:05.680
won't get you in trouble?

00:38:05.680 --> 00:38:07.080
- Well, it could
(Mark clears throat)

00:38:07.080 --> 00:38:09.581
if they find me I suppose, but it's not--

00:38:09.581 --> 00:38:11.353
- [Mark] But you move
around like you said.

00:38:13.400 --> 00:38:15.440
- Facebook everybody knows where I'm at,

00:38:15.440 --> 00:38:17.210
it's not like I'm hiding that much.

00:38:17.210 --> 00:38:19.153
I don't like running.

00:38:21.200 --> 00:38:23.367
I am running, but I'm not.

00:38:24.320 --> 00:38:27.844
I don't wanna say, "Here's
where I'm staying at here,

00:38:27.844 --> 00:38:28.960
"Come get me."

00:38:28.960 --> 00:38:29.793
But...

00:38:34.683 --> 00:38:36.833
It is what it is, I guess.

00:38:39.179 --> 00:38:41.367
(Ally sniffling)
- Well.

00:38:41.367 --> 00:38:44.620
Well Ally thank you so much
for sharing your story.

00:38:44.620 --> 00:38:49.620
- Yeah, thank you.
(Ally sniffling)

00:38:50.290 --> 00:38:52.440
- [Mark] What do you
think in your childhood

00:38:52.440 --> 00:38:57.440
was the most powerful factor
in leading you down this path?

00:39:02.299 --> 00:39:04.212
(Ally sighing)

00:39:04.212 --> 00:39:06.295
- That's a good question.

00:39:07.800 --> 00:39:10.960
I had a lot of things that happened

00:39:10.960 --> 00:39:12.730
to me that were traumatic

00:39:12.730 --> 00:39:15.153
and at the same time, I
had a really good life.

00:39:17.080 --> 00:39:21.890
I had horses, I competed
ballroom and Latin dancing,

00:39:21.890 --> 00:39:24.280
I had a lot of really great things.

00:39:24.280 --> 00:39:27.730
But then like I said, times
were different in the '80s.

00:39:27.730 --> 00:39:30.950
I also had uncles and
aunts and family members

00:39:30.950 --> 00:39:33.631
that used drugs, dealt drugs, grew drugs,

00:39:33.631 --> 00:39:38.631
and I wanted to be part of it all.

00:39:39.313 --> 00:39:41.880
I wanted to be part of it all.

00:39:41.880 --> 00:39:44.590
And I liked it.

00:39:44.590 --> 00:39:48.070
I liked the bad stuff.

00:39:48.070 --> 00:39:49.373
I had fun with it.

00:39:50.980 --> 00:39:53.589
I guess I was just always
a bad seed I guess.

00:39:53.589 --> 00:39:56.040
But in a good way, I'm
a loving good person,

00:39:56.040 --> 00:39:56.873
I have a good heart,

00:39:56.873 --> 00:40:01.800
but I'm a street person too, I
like the streets, it's weird.

00:40:05.160 --> 00:40:08.390
But probably the biggest thing

00:40:08.390 --> 00:40:13.140
was the fact that I had
drugs readily available

00:40:13.140 --> 00:40:15.140
and people willing to give
them to me at a young age.

00:40:15.140 --> 00:40:18.130
And I wanted to be part
of what they were doing.

00:40:18.130 --> 00:40:19.430
My aunts and uncles were cool.

00:40:19.430 --> 00:40:22.632
My aunt was beautiful,
my uncle was handsome.

00:40:22.632 --> 00:40:23.465
(Ally sniffing)

00:40:23.465 --> 00:40:25.870
And they had lots of
friends, tons of friends,

00:40:25.870 --> 00:40:27.970
and I just wanted to be part of all of it.

00:40:28.980 --> 00:40:31.480
Where my grandparents lived in Fairbanks,

00:40:31.480 --> 00:40:33.410
there's not very many
kids in that neighborhood,

00:40:33.410 --> 00:40:35.060
they're kinda out in the boonies.

00:40:36.740 --> 00:40:38.810
So what there was a lot of was teenagers,

00:40:38.810 --> 00:40:39.830
drugs, and partying.

00:40:39.830 --> 00:40:43.050
And Alaska, I don't
wanna raise my daughter

00:40:43.050 --> 00:40:43.890
or my kids there.

00:40:43.890 --> 00:40:47.530
My son is already, okay he just turned 18,

00:40:47.530 --> 00:40:48.620
he just got out of prison.

00:40:48.620 --> 00:40:51.160
He's been in prison since he was 13.

00:40:51.160 --> 00:40:53.623
So he's already following
down my footsteps.

00:40:54.960 --> 00:40:56.313
And I don't want that for my daughter.

00:40:56.313 --> 00:41:00.361
And I know that drugs
are everywhere you go,

00:41:00.361 --> 00:41:02.420
but (Ally sniffling) in Alaska

00:41:02.420 --> 00:41:04.758
there's not a whole lot of diversity.

00:41:04.758 --> 00:41:06.870
There's a lot of darkness,

00:41:06.870 --> 00:41:10.152
a lot of cold, and a lot of
depression, and a lot of drugs.

00:41:10.152 --> 00:41:11.420
(Ally laughing)

00:41:11.420 --> 00:41:15.500
So people and the kids, that's
what they get into there.

00:41:15.500 --> 00:41:18.670
Unless you're really, I don't know,

00:41:18.670 --> 00:41:22.220
unless you have some amazing
support maybe with your family

00:41:22.220 --> 00:41:25.650
do you not, but I think
at least 70% of the kids

00:41:25.650 --> 00:41:27.320
probably fall into drugs there.

00:41:27.320 --> 00:41:30.220
And I don't think that my
kids will be any different.

00:41:30.220 --> 00:41:32.343
My daughter might be
because (Ally sniffling)

00:41:32.343 --> 00:41:35.330
because she's had a
rough, tough little life.

00:41:35.330 --> 00:41:38.220
She's just the best hearted
little soul in the world.

00:41:38.220 --> 00:41:42.610
And I don't believe she
will get into drugs ever

00:41:42.610 --> 00:41:46.503
because she's watched me and how it's,

00:41:47.510 --> 00:41:48.780
and she loves me to death.

00:41:48.780 --> 00:41:51.768
But she knows what my problem is.

00:41:51.768 --> 00:41:54.447
She knows that I have a drug issue.

00:41:54.447 --> 00:41:57.930
(car engine rumbling)
And someday,

00:41:57.930 --> 00:42:00.200
maybe she's gonna hate me for that.

00:42:00.200 --> 00:42:03.420
And I hope not, but I
wouldn't blame her if she did

00:42:03.420 --> 00:42:08.420
because I've always, it
seems like I put drugs first.

00:42:08.730 --> 00:42:13.730
But I am putting her and the kids first.

00:42:13.740 --> 00:42:16.140
I put my last son first

00:42:16.140 --> 00:42:20.840
by giving him to a mom I know wanted him

00:42:20.840 --> 00:42:23.993
and would make him feel
like he was a gift to her.

00:42:24.860 --> 00:42:25.693
He was.

00:42:26.650 --> 00:42:29.780
I don't wanna ruin my
kids' lives the way I have,

00:42:29.780 --> 00:42:30.613
but I have.

00:42:34.460 --> 00:42:36.503
But with my childhood
is definitely probably

00:42:36.503 --> 00:42:38.797
because the drugs were readily available,

00:42:38.797 --> 00:42:40.620
very readily available.

00:42:40.620 --> 00:42:42.930
And it's depressing,
nothing to do in Alaska.

00:42:42.930 --> 00:42:45.297
Very cold (Ally chuckles) very dark.

00:42:45.297 --> 00:42:46.330
(Ally sniffling)

00:42:46.330 --> 00:42:47.320
Except for in the summertime,

00:42:47.320 --> 00:42:49.710
then it's light all the time.
(Ally laughing)

00:42:49.710 --> 00:42:50.620
But...

00:42:51.640 --> 00:42:52.473
- [Mark] All right Ally.

00:42:52.473 --> 00:42:53.853
Well thank you so much for talking to me.

00:42:53.853 --> 00:42:55.210
- Thank you.
- And good luck with--

00:42:55.210 --> 00:42:57.123
- With everything?
- With everything.

00:42:57.123 --> 00:42:58.573
(Ally laughing)
- Thank you.

